{% doc %}
  One image for a customizable section or block, from either an upload or an
  external URL, with a shared aspect-ratio control.

  UPLOAD IS THE GOOD PATH. A picked image goes through Shopify's CDN, which
  is what makes the responsive ladder work — the whole srcset/sizes system
  that was tuned so retina screens get enough pixels. An external URL cannot
  be resized, so it renders as a single flat file at whatever size the remote
  host serves; it exists because it was asked for, not because it is equal.
  When both are set the upload wins.

  SHAPE IS AN ASPECT RATIO, NOT A RADIUS. The brand is square-cornered
  everywhere, so this deliberately exposes no corner control.

  @param {object} [image] - image_picker value (preferred)
  @param {string} [image_url] - external image URL, used only when no upload
  @param {string} [draft_asset] - theme asset filename, the existing draft
    fallback (see draft-image)
  @param {string} img_class - class for the <img>
  @param {string} [sizes] - responsive sizes attribute for the uploaded path
  @param {string} [ratio] - "756/957" | "1/1" | "3/2" | "4/5"; omitted leaves
    whatever the stylesheet already sets
  @param {string} [alt]
  @param {string} [loading] - "lazy" (default) or "eager"
  @param {number} [asset_width] - intrinsic width of the draft asset, also the
    reserved width for an external URL (its real size is unknowable server-side)
  @param {number} [asset_height] - intrinsic height of the draft asset
  @example
  {% render 'media-image', image: block.settings.image, image_url: block.settings.image_url, img_class: 'image-card__media', ratio: block.settings.ratio %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign load = loading | default: 'lazy'
  assign alt_text = alt | default: ''
  assign ratio_style = ''
  if ratio != blank
    assign ratio_style = 'aspect-ratio: ' | append: ratio | append: ';'
  endif
-%}

{%- if image == blank and image_url != blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    width/height reserve the box so the page does not shift while a remote
    file loads. The real dimensions cannot be read server-side, so these are
    the container's own proportions — the CSS ratio governs the rendered box
    either way, and object-fit handles whatever actually arrives.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <img
    src="{{ image_url }}"
    class="{{ img_class }}"
    alt="{{ alt_text | escape }}"
    loading="{{ load }}"
    width="{{ asset_width | default: 756 }}"
    height="{{ asset_height | default: 957 }}"
    {% if ratio_style != blank %}
      style="{{ ratio_style }}"
    {% endif %}
  >
{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    No wrapper element: the ratio is handed to draft-image so it lands on the
    <img> itself. Adding a span here would change the DOM these grids depend
    on (.image-card__frame > img), which is exactly the kind of silent layout
    change this phase is not allowed to make.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% render 'draft-image',
    image: image,
    draft_asset: draft_asset,
    img_class: img_class,
    sizes: sizes,
    alt: alt_text,
    loading: load,
    ratio: ratio,
    asset_width: asset_width,
    asset_height: asset_height
  %}
{%- endif -%}
